  ia_jackson: { publisher: "unverified", publisherName: "ArcGIS Online account jesstracy (Parcels, FeatureServer 0 — org jackson49; the account is not tied to the county by its profile)", verifiedOn: V2, verifiedNote: "MEASURED live from this sandbox 2026-10-29 (host is *.arcgis.com): polygon layer, 22,056 features, extent inside Jackson County; 5 of 5 spread points across the county and 4 of 4 points beside its county lines returned a polygon with parcel id PIN and owner DEEDHOLD (the situs column is blank on the rural lots sampled); the layer's data was last edited 2019-07-09 (the item was re-saved 2022-06). Found by the second pass: the first pass refused it on a 2020 currency floor that the owner's 2026-10-28 copy rule replaced (older is fine if it is the best there is); it beats the 2017 statewide copy by two years and carries acreage, the owner and the legal description." },
  ia_monroe: { publisher: "own", publisherName: "Monroe County GIS (ArcGIS Online pfreshwater, Monroe_Features layer 43 \u2014 the county's published parcel join; viewer rebuilt by Sidwell July 2025)", verifiedOn: V2, verifiedNote: "MEASURED live from this sandbox 2026-10-29 (host is *.arcgis.com): polygon layer, 33,176 rows over 15,254 distinct parcel numbers, extent inside Monroe County; 5 of 5 spread points across the county and 4 of 4 points beside its county lines returned a polygon with parcel id PIN, owner PRIMARY_NAME1 and situs ADDRESS (a rural lot reads 000000, read as no address); the layer was last edited 2026-07-08. The county's published join stacks TWO rows on every lot — the original export (OBJECTID 1–16,599, previous owner) and the re-import (16,600 and up, current owner), e.g. PIN 711712200001 reads Asher, Elsie O \u2014 1/2 Interest/Life Tenant, then Francis Properties, LLC — so the row declares pointOrderBy \"OBJECTID DESC\" (newest row first) and the id search lists one lot once. Found by the second pass: a county-account tiles service (CadastralAnnotation) led to the same org's FeatureServer; the first pass's title / extent search never opened it." },
  ia_carroll: { publisher: "own", publisherName: "Carroll County GIS (ArcGIS Online Sarah_CarrollCountyGIS, ParcelPoly1 \u2014 the county GIS account that also publishes the county zoning and floodplain maps)", verifiedOn: V2, verifiedNote: "MEASURED live from this sandbox 2026-10-29 (host is *.arcgis.com): polygon layer, 22,355 rows over 22,044 distinct parcel numbers, extent inside Carroll County; 5 of 5 spread points across the county and 4 of 4 points beside its county lines returned a polygon with parcel id PIN, owner DEEDNAME and situs ADDRESS (blank on most rural lots); a Carroll city lot (N Adams St) reads its commercial parcel; the layer's data was last edited 2025-09-02. Found by the second pass: the county GIS account's zoning and floodplain web maps sit in Carroll's box and the org's other service, ParcelPoly1, was never listed by the first pass's title search." },
  ia_vanburen: { publisher: "own", publisherName: "Van Buren County GIS (ArcGIS Online vbcogis, Master layer 17 ParcelPoly_GISINFO \u2014 the county GIS account that also publishes the county sections, roads, soils and voting precincts)", verifiedOn: V2, verifiedNote: "MEASURED live from this sandbox 2026-10-29 (host is *.arcgis.com): polygon layer, 15,127 rows over 14,462 distinct parcel numbers, extent inside Van Buren County; 5 of 5 spread points across the county and 3 of 4 points beside its county lines (the miss is the Des Moines River border) returned a polygon with parcel id PIN, owner PRIMARY_NAME1 and situs ADDRESS (a rural lot reads 000000, read as no address); the layer was last edited 2026-07-01. Found by the second pass: the county GIS account (vbcogis) publishes one multi-layer FeatureServer titled just 'Master' — parcel polygons are layer 17 ParcelPoly_GISINFO — which no name search for parcels or for the county surfaced." },
  ia_tama: { publisher: "third-party", publisherName: "a Drake University GIS-class project on ArcGIS Online (account kate.bachmann@drake.edu, service Tama_County_Roads layer 2 \u2014 a copy of the county assessor's 2026 export)", verifiedOn: V2, verifiedNote: "MEASURED live from this sandbox 2026-10-29 (host is *.arcgis.com): polygon layer, 22,980 rows over 22,370 distinct parcel numbers, extent inside Tama County; 5 of 5 spread points across the county and 4 of 4 points beside its county lines returned a polygon with parcel id PIN, owner OwnerName and situs FullSitus (blank on most rural lots); TaxYear 2026, the layer was last edited 2026-03-30. NOT the county's own: it is the 'TamaCo03272026' layer inside a Drake University GIS-class project service (Tama_County_Roads, ArcGIS Online account kate.bachmann@drake.edu), carrying the county assessor's own export fields (TscID, TaxYear, ParcelType, DistrictsA, TifDistric). Found by the second pass's exhaustive service enumeration: no name or county search surfaces a service titled 'Tama_County_Roads'. It is a student project, so it may be removed — the 2017 statewide copy (docs) is the fallback to re-wire if it is." },
